<section>
	<h1>About the App</h1>
	<p>
		<strong>Buy Later</strong> helps prevent impulse purchases in today's modern online shopping environment.
	</p>
	<p>
		Have you ever spontaneously bought something and then a few days later realized you didn't actually want or need it?
	</p>
	<p>
		It can be easy to open an app and buy something in under a minute. <strong>Buy Later</strong> is designed to
		create a buffer in that moment. The app provides a minimal, clean interface where you can list things you want
		as you think of them - once they make it through the fixed hold period, you can safely buy them (if you still think
		it's a good idea).
	</p>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Features</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Minimalist user interface</li>
		<li>Fixed 10, 20, or 30 day hold period</li>
		<li>Notifications when an item's timer completes (optional)</li>
		<li>100% ad-free, no sign-in, and no accounts</li>
		<li>Private: data is only stored on your device</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>System Requirements</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>iPhone iOS 14.0 or later</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
	<dl>
		<dt>Where is my data stored?</dt>
		<dd>
			All data is stored locally on your device and is not accessible anywhere else. If you delete the app, all data is lost.
		</dd>
	</dl>
</section>


<section>
	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p>
		Buy Later is committed to protecting your privacy. We do not require an account and we do not collect personal
		information. All content is stored locally on your device.
	</p>
	<p>
		The app makes only two limited network requests, described below: an anonymous usage ping when it launches, and
		a feedback message that is sent only if you choose to submit one. Neither includes the contents of your saved
		items.
	</p>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Data Storage</h2>
	<p>
		All information is saved in secure on-device storage on your device.
	</p>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Usage Ping</h2>
	<p>
		When the app launches, it sends a single anonymous "ping" to our feedback service so we can gauge how many
		times the app is opened. This request contains only a fixed source label identifying the app
		(<code>buy-later-ios</code>); it includes no account, no personal information, and none of your item content. It
		cannot be used to track or identify you across apps or over time. It is equivalent to trying to go to the url <a
			href="https://feedback.k1apps.dev/ping?source=buy-later-ios">https://feedback.k1apps.dev/ping?source=buy-later-ios</a>.
	</p>
	<h3>Example of a ping:</h3>
	<pre>
		<code>
	useEffect(() => {
		fetch("https://feedback.k1apps.dev/ping?source=buy-later-ios", {
			method: "GET",
		}).catch(() => {});
	}, []);
		</code>
	</pre>
</section>

<section>
	<h2>Feedback Submissions</h2>
	<p>
		The app includes an optional feedback form. Nothing is sent unless you fill it out and tap Send. When you do,
		your typed message is delivered to the developer along with a small amount of technical info to help
		diagnose issues:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>your message text</li>
		<li>your email address - only if you choose to enter one for a reply (otherwise none is sent)</li>
		<li>the app version and build number</li>
		<li>your device model and iOS version</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Your saved items and other in-app data are never included. Feedback you submit is retained by the
		developer so we can read and respond to it.
	</p>
	<h3>Example of data:</h3>
	<pre>
		<code>
	App: buy-later-ios
	Submitted: 2026-05-30 04:17 UTC
	Reply-To: not provided

	Message:
	I love the app, thanks.

	Metadata:
	version: 1.0.1
	build: 3
	commit: f197b74
	platform: iOS 26.5
	device: iPhone 16 Pro
		</code>
	</pre>
</section>

